                    <p class=MsoNormal><span style="font-family:仿宋;mso-bidi-font-family:'Times New Roman';font-size:12.0000pt;
mso-font-kerning:1.0000pt;"><font face="仿宋"><p>《Regional Anatomy of the Head and Neck》 is a fundamental course for undergraduate students major in stomatology, focusing on the systematic study of the anatomical structures of the head and neck. Through a combination of theoretical lectures and practical exercises, the course aims to deepen students' understanding of the morphology, location, function, and interrelationships of these structures, laying a solid anatomical foundation for subsequent clinical studies.</p></font></span><span style="font-family:'Times New Roman';mso-fareast-font-family:仿宋;font-size:10.5000pt;
mso-font-kerning:1.0000pt;"><o:p></o:p></span></p>
                </td>
            </tr>
            <tr style="height:19.9000pt;">
                <td width=777 valign=center colspan=14 style="width:466.7000pt;padding:0.0000pt 5.4000pt 0.0000pt 5.4000pt ;border-left:1.0000pt solid windowtext;
